hf-xet 1.8.0 on Android: TLS roots from the device's system CA store, not rustls-platform-verifier.

reqwest 0.13's rustls backend verifies through rustls-platform-verifier unless the client is built with
`tls_certs_only`. On Android that verifier needs `init_hosted(JNIEnv, Context)` and its Java classes, which a
Python app never provides, so every hf_xet download panicked with "Expect rustls-platform-verifier to be
initialized" (torchnative, Galaxy Z Flip4, 2026-11-27). On Android only, both of xet-client's reqwest builders
now get `tls_certs_only(<the system store's certificates>)`. The store rule is python-multiplatform's (its
#549, SPEC L-5b), so the app's Python ssl and hf_xet trust the same CAs: /apex/com.android.conscrypt/cacerts
(Android 14+, the updatable store) if it holds certificates, else /system/etc/security/cacerts, never merged.
User-installed CAs are not read. Other targets are unchanged. Approved by the team lead, 2026-11-27.

